<p>Those two integers are PDF object numbers, and they are the numbers the compiled catalog references.</p>
<p>A document may hold as many named forms as needed; their indices combine into the one form dictionary
the catalog points at. A <code>contact</code> form and a <code>billing</code> form with one field each produce
<code>&lt;&lt;/Fields[5 0 R 6 0 R]&gt;&gt;</code>, with <code>getFieldIndices()</code> returning <code>[5]</code> on the first and <code>[6]</code> on the
second — the reader sees one flat set.</p>
<p>One form also gathers fields from as many pages as the document has, so a questionnaire running over
several sheets is still one form:</p>
